.SH NAME
messq-serve - run the messq daemon


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq serve [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the messq daemon against a data directory, serving the HTTP API over a
Unix socket or loopback TCP.

.PP
serve keeps its own section-8 flag set and its own environment
fallbacks; it exits 74 when storage latched read-only, 75 when the
data directory is locked by another daemon, and 78 when the
configuration can never work — systemd's RestartPreventExitStatus
depends on those values.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for serve


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq serve --data-dir /var/lib/messq # noexec: starts a long-running daemon
  messq serve --listen tcp://127.0.0.1:4390 # noexec: starts a long-running daemon
.EE


